ns\nL169:   * 【9†Search in PubMed】\nL170:   * 【10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL171:   * 【3†Add to Search】\nL172: \nL173: . 2019 Jan 9;19(1):369-374.\nL174: \nL175: doi: 10.1021/acs.nanolett.8b04051. Epub 2018 Dec 10.\nL176: # Molecular Threading-Dependent Mass Transport in Paper Origami for Single-Step Electrochemical DNA Sensors\nL177: \nL178: 【11†Dekai Ye】^{  【12†1】   【13†2】 }, 【14†Li Li】^{  【15†3】 }, 【16†Zhenhua Li】^{  【13†2】 }, 【17†Yueyue Zhang】^{  【13†2】 }, 【18†Min Li】^{  【12†1】 }, 【19†Jiye Shi】^{  【13†2】 }, 【20†Lihua Wang】^{  【13†2】   【21†4】 }, 【22†Chunhai Fan】^{  【23†5】   【13†2】 }, 【24†Jinghua Yu】^{  【15†3】 }, 【25†Xiaolei Zuo】^{  【12†1】   【23†5】 }\nL179: \nL180: Affiliations Expand\nL181: ### Affiliations\nL182:   * ^{1} Institute of Molecular Medicine, Renji Hospital, School of Medicine , Shanghai Jiao Tong University , Shanghai 200127 , China.\nL183:   * ^{2} Division of Physical Biology and Bioimaging Center, Shanghai Synchrotron Radiation Facility (SSRF), CAS Key Laboratory of Interficial Physics and Technology , Shanghai Institute of Applied Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences , Shanghai 201800 , China.\nL184:   * ^{3} School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering , University of Jinan , Jinan 250022 , China.\nL185:   * ^{4} Shanghai Key Laboratory of Green Chemistry and Chemical Processes, School of Chemistry and Molecular Engineering , East China Normal University , Shanghai 200241 , China.\nL186:   * ^{5} School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering , Shanghai Jiao Tong University , Shanghai 200240 , China.\nL187:   * PMID: 30511869\nL188:   * DOI: 【26†10.1021/acs.nanolett.8b04051†doi.org】\nL189: \nL190: Item in Clipboard\nL191: # Molecular Threading-Dependent Mass Transport in Paper Origami for Single-Step Electrochemical DNA Sensors\nL192: \nL193: Dekai Ye et al. Nano Lett. 2019.\nL194: \nL195: Show details\nL196: \nL197: Display options\nL198: \nL199: Display options\nL200: \nL201: Format [Select]\nL202: \nL203: [Button: Nano Lett ]\nL204: \nL205: Actions\nL206: \nL207:   * 【9†Search in PubMed】\nL208:   * 【10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL209:   * 【3†Add to Search】\nL210: \nL211: . 2019 Jan 9;19(1):369-374.\nL212: \nL213: doi: 10.1021/acs.nanolett.8b04051. Epub 2018 Dec 10.\nL214: ### Authors\nL215: \nL216: 【11†Dekai Ye】^{  【27†1】   【28†2】 }, 【14†Li Li】^{  【29†3】 }, 【16†Zhenhua Li】^{  【28†2】 }, 【17†Yueyue Zhang】^{  【28†2】 }, 【18†Min Li】^{  【27†1】 }, 【19†Jiye Shi】^{  【28†2】 }, 【20†Lihua Wang】^{  【28†2】   【30†4】 }, 【22†Chunhai Fan】^{  【31†5】   【28†2】 }, 【24†Jinghua Yu】^{  【29†3】 }, 【25†Xiaolei Zuo】^{  【27†1】   【31†5】 }\nL217: ### Affiliations\nL218:   * ^{1} Institute of Molecular Medicine, Renji Hospital, School of Medicine , Shanghai Jiao Tong University , Shanghai 200127 , China.\nL219:   * ^{2} Division of Physical Biology and Bioimaging Center, Shanghai Synchrotron Radiation Facility (SSRF), CAS Key Laboratory of Interficial Physics and Technology , Shanghai Institute of Applied Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences , Shanghai 201800 , China.\nL220:   * ^{3} School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering , University of Jinan , Jinan 250022 , China.\nL221:   * ^{4} Shanghai Key Laboratory of Green Chemistry and Chemical Processes, School of Chemistry and Molecular Engineering , East China Normal University , Shanghai 200241 , China.\nL222:   * ^{5} School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering , Shanghai Jiao Tong University , Shanghai 200240 , China.\nL223:   * PMID: 30511869\nL224:   * DOI: 【26†10.1021/acs.nanolett.8b04051†doi.org】\nL225: \nL226: Item in Clipboard\nL227: \nL228: [Button: Full text links ]Cite\nL229: \nL230: Display options\nL231: \nL232: Display options\nL233: \nL234: Format [Select]\nL235: ## Abstract\nL236: Molecular transport controls the efficiency of complex biological network systems such as cellular signaling system and cascade biomedical reaction. However, device fabrication for molecular sensing is often restricted by a low transport efficiency and complicated processing. Here, we report a molecular threading-dependent transport system using three-dimensional (3D) paper origami enabling the directional transport of biomolecules.\nL237: We demonstrate that framework nucleic acid-based interface engineering allows orthogonal molecular recognition and enzymatic reaction with programmed order on site. We thus develop a single-step electrochemical DNA sensor for quantitative analysis with 1 picomolar sensitivity within 60 min. Our sensor can discriminate a mismatched target at the level of a single base mismatch.\nL238: Our study shows a great potential toward the development of a biomimetic molecular transport system for point-of-care and precision diagnosis.\nL239: Keywords: Molecular threading; framework nucleic acid; mass transport; single-step electrochemical biosensing; three-dimensional (3D) paper origami.\nL240: \nL241: 【32†PubMed Disclaimer】\nL242: ## Publication types\nL243: \nL244:   * [Button: Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't ]\nL245: \nL246: Actions\nL247: \nL248:     * 【33†Search in PubMed】\nL249:     * 【34†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL250:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL251: ## MeSH terms\nL252: \nL253:   * [Button: Biological Transport / genetics ]\nL254: \nL255: Actions\nL256: \nL257:     * 【35†Search in PubMed】\nL258:     * 【36†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL259:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL260: \nL261:   * [Button: Biosensing Techniques* ]\nL262: \nL263: Actions\nL264: \nL265:     * 【37†Search in PubMed】\nL266:     * 【38†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL267:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL268: \nL269:   * [Button: DNA / chemistry ]\nL270: \nL271: Actions\nL272: \nL273:     * 【39†Search in PubMed】\nL274:     * 【40†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL275:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL276: \nL277:   * [Button: DNA / isolation & purification* ]\nL278: Actions\nL279: \nL280:     * 【41†Search in PubMed】\nL281:     * 【40†Search in MeSH†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL282:     * 【3†Add to Search】\nL28